&amp;#x200B;

Why do I watch movies ? Good question. The motive seems to have changed for me over time. But basically it has been to augment my otherwise spartan life. It's been troubled for the most part, so escapism is the main reason. I was one of those broken home kids who was basically confused and frightened, and movies were a break from that. And my Mom brought me to movies rather than get a sitter. The first movies I remember besides the usual westerns and monster movies were Elias Kazan's 'East of Eden', Hitchcock's 'The Man Who Knew Too Much' and 'Vertigo' and Nicholas Ray's 'Rebel Without a Cause'. Those set the stage. I suppose I liked the Elvis Presley ones alright, but I knew they weren't serious, even then.

So Nicholas Ray and Alfred Hitchcock more or less molded my aesthetic. Both of them were interested in identity, so that was appealing. And I always looked for similar movies. Back in the day it was written reviews for the most part. Then trailers on TV, and at the theater. After awhile I got a sense of the movies I would like, directors, actors and so on. But that sense of an alternate life has always been there.

I like a sense of mystery surrounding stories. As a student of the paranormal I lean toward movies dealing with that, just to get ideas about it.

I have to say that the work of Nicolas Roeg, David Lynch and David Cronenberg have been quite pleasing for me in the latter half of my life.

&gt;We all do it;

No, we don't.

And if I find myself watching something bad, I turn it off. Life is too short for anything worse than 7/10.

Sometimes there's a lot to learn about how storytelling does or doesn't work when you watch it fail.

The last season of Game of Thrones is a great example.  Acting, top notch. Costumes and music, A+.  But when you start to look at the writing you can really lay out exactly what the problems are and you can learn a lot about 'what are and are not reasonable expectations' when watching that debacle.

For example if you've established a character for 7 seasons to be incredibly deliberate in their handling of executions, &gt;!it makes no sense if they just fly off the handle and warcrime an entire city in the second to last episode!&lt;
